WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.320
Every   useful   voice  

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.680
AI   project   starts  

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.320
with   a   business  

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.400
question.   In   HarborVoice,  

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.260
that   question   is  

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.640
simple:   where   is  

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.080
my   shipment?   The  

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:10.880
terminal   and   its  

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:11.981
records   are   fictional.  

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.840
The   engineering   boundaries  

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.520
are   real.   Nora  

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.079
asks   for   an  

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:17.680
exact   reference,   then  

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.500
calls   the   shipment  

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.900
lookup   tool.   A  

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.420
recorded   customs   hold  

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.360
stays   a   customs  

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.880
hold.   An   estimated  

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.040
arrival   stays   an  

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.580
estimate.   The   knowledge  

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.920
base   explains   published  

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.360
procedures,   while   tool  

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.400
results   provide   the  

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.980
shipment   facts.   If  

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.200
a   lookup   fails,  

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.180
Nora   must   say  

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.260
so.   If   the  

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.540
customer   needs   help,  

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.560
the   assistant   prepares  

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.300
a   request   for  

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.080
human   review.   Pending  

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.000
review   does   not  

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.720
mean   approved,   transferred  

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.160
or   released.   The  

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.360
public   visitor   agent  

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.280
has   a   separate,  

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.520
read-only   tool   and  

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.420
a   bounded   trial  

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.160
window.   The   engineering  

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.680
workspace   adds   versioned  

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.020
scenarios,   provider   simulations  

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.160
and   explicit   failure  

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.020
cases.   These   results  

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.120
describe   the   tests  

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:58.701
that   were   run;  

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.720
they   do   not  

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.980
promise   perfect   future  

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.080
conversations.   Explore   the  

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.019
working   demonstration,   inspect  

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:05.879
the   source   and  

00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:06.921
compare   the   evidence.  

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.260
HarborVoice   brings   voice,  

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.300
knowledge   and   human  

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.580
control   into   one  

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.860
transparent   workflow.
